\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2835:          (let [id (check-ref! state :cell/set! :cell-ref (:cell effect))]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2852:          :cell/new-provenance\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2855:                          {:reason :nil-provenance, :effect :cell/new-provenance}))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:216:(defn- mint-cell\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:241:(defn- cursor-cell\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:252:(defn- cell-identity\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:312:(defn- call-out-cell\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/remote.cljc:539:(defn- cell-resources\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc:392:(defn- walk-cells\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc:418:(defn- item-cells\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc:537:(defn- unnumbered-cells\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc:609:(defn- spell-cell\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc:1427:(defn- cell!\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc:1435:(defn- cell-for!\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/reader.cljc:182:(defn- cell-of\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/reader.cljc:195:(defn- cell-candidates\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/provenance_scope.cljc:16:            [521 :cell/new-provenance] [692 :cell/provenance]]}\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/provenance_scope.cljc:20:            [818 :cell/new-provenance] [1100 :cell/provenance]]}\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/provenance_scope.cljc:24:            [521 :cell/new-provenance] [692 :cell/provenance]]}})\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/provenance_scope.cljc:27:  {'cell/dsg__new-provenance :cell/new-provenance\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc:2487:(defn- rebuilt-cell\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:678:Runtime-allocated mutable locations are not AST nodes. They are the `cell` host module's `cell/new`, `cell/get`, `cell/set!` and `cell/authentic?`, ordinary applications whose effects the engine interprets on all four VMs. `cell/new` answers a sealed `{:type :cell-ref :id :cell-N :seal s}`; the content lives in the task's `:heap` (see `state.md`), never in the named store. `cell/authentic?` is the ruling-of-record pure query (yang.antlr.md 8.10.12): the heap's own yes-or-no on a candidate reference, answered as data where `cell/get` would fail closed.\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:680:**Reclamation.** The heap is collected (Architect heap-reclamation design, slice 1; this supersedes the cell ruling's \"heap reclamation can wait\"). The `:cell/new` effect counts allocations, and when the count reaches the threshold it runs a deterministic, stop-the-world mark-sweep before allocating:\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md:121:**Purpose:** `:heap` holds the task's cells, the mutable locations `cell/new` allocates and a sealed `:cell-ref` reaches. It is VM state, not continuation state: a write is seen by every holder of the ref and survives continuation re-entry (box semantics). `:gc` is its collector's state. Both are declared record fields wherever a VM is a positional record, and both start empty in every constructor and `spawn-module` child.\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md:123:**Provenance:** an entry may carry an optional private `:provenance` sibling beside `:value` and `:seal`, written only by the privileged mint (`cell/dsg__new-provenance`, effect `:cell/new-provenance`) at allocation, never attached, replaced, or cleared afterwards. The VM treats it as opaque data — no frontend dispatch, no reason matching, no rendering — and answers it only through the authenticated private reader (`cell/dsg__provenance`, effect `:cell/provenance`), which returns nil for anything else and is never fatal. `cell/get` returns only `:value`; `cell/set!` and `heap-write` preserve `:provenance` while updating `:value`/`:seal`. The collector traces `:provenance` as data from every live entry, from pinned entries, and as an extra root at allocation, so payload cells referenced only by a retained provenance stay reachable while the wrapper is, and become collectible when the wrapper drops.\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md:125:**Reclamation:** deterministic, allocation-triggered, stop-the-world mark-sweep, tracing kernel positions and value positions in two modes (`ast.md` Part 6),, a pure `vm -> vm'` (`yin.vm.engine/collect`). `:since` counts allocations; when it reaches `:threshold`, the `:cell/new` effect collects before allocating, and the threshold becomes `max(:base, 2 x live)`. `:base` is a composition parameter (`:gc-threshold`, default 4096). Marking runs over the heap as it was when the cycle began, and the sweep removes only ids of that snapshot, so an id allocated at or after the cycle's counter start is spared; a budgeted marker can later reuse it. `:pinned` holds cells whose refs left the VM's view on a stream or in an FFI request; they stay live for the task's life. Ids are never reused (`:id-counter` only grows), and a ref to a swept cell is refused with `:dead-or-forged-reference`. This supersedes the cell ruling's \"heap reclamation can wait\".\n(ns yang.rt.effect-test\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n            [yang.clojure :as clj]\n            [yang.clojure.prelude :as prelude]\n            [yang.core.call :as call]\n            [yang.core.uast :as u]\n            [yang.rt.effect :as effect]\n            [yang.rt.int :as int-rt]\n            [yang.typescript.antlr.linked-harness :as h]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.integer :as integer]\n            [yin.vm.linker.interpreter :as link]\n            [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]))\n\n\n(def ^:private registry (prelude/admit (h/registry)))\n\n(def ^:private published\n  (delay\n    (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n          install (fn [spec]\n                    (let [result (publish/publish-module! store spec)]\n                      (or (:address result)\n                          (throw (ex-info \"Publication refused\" result)))))\n          call-address (install (call/module-spec registry))\n          effect-address (install (effect/module-spec registry))\n          int-address (install (int-rt/module-spec registry effect-address))\n          clj-address (install (prelude/module-spec registry call-address effect-address))]\n      (link/composition\n        {:content-store store\n         :derivation :trusted\n         :name-env {'yang.call call-address 'yrt.effect effect-address\n                    'yrt.int int-address 'clj clj-address}}))))\n\n\n(defn- run-runtime [backend bundled? form]\n  (let [body (u/sexp->uast form)]\n    (vm/value\n      (h/run-linked backend\n        (if bundled?\n          (u/mark-tails (u/seq-nodes [effect/uast int-rt/uast body]))\n          (u/then (u/sexp->uast '(require 'yrt.int)) body))\n        {:modules registry :link-source @published}))))\n\n\n(deftest abortive-control\n  (let [form\n        '(let [ctx (cell/new (yrt.effect/ctx nil 0 0 nil))\n               log (cell/new [])\n               note (fn [v] (cell/set! log (conj (cell/get log) v)))\n               on-empty (fn [e] (conj [] :empty e))\n               normal (yrt.effect/try-value ctx (fn [] :normal) note)\n               orelse (yrt.effect/try-orelse ctx (fn [] :ignored)\n                        note (fn [] :orelse))\n               raised (yrt.effect/try-value ctx\n                        (fn []\n                          (yrt.effect/try-finally ctx\n                            (fn []\n                              (yrt.effect/handle ctx :unrelated\n                                (fn [payload k] (note :unexpected-handler))\n                                (fn []\n                                  (yrt.effect/try-finally ctx\n                                    (fn [] (yrt.effect/raise ctx :boom on-empty))\n                                    (fn [e] (note (conj [] :inner e)))\n                                    :inner-normal))))\n                            (fn [e] (note (conj [] :outer e)))\n                            :outer-normal))\n                        (fn [e] (conj [] :caught e)))\n               normal-finally (yrt.effect/try-finally ctx\n                                (fn [] 3) note :finally-normal)\n               ec (yrt.effect/call-ec ctx\n                    (fn [exit]\n                      (yrt.effect/try-finally ctx (fn [] (exit 4)) note :unused))\n                    :escape)\n               terminal (yrt.effect/call-terminal ctx\n                          (fn [exit]\n                            (yrt.effect/try-finally ctx (fn [] (exit 5)) note :unused)))]\n           (conj [] normal orelse raised normal-finally ec terminal\n                 (cell/get log) (yrt.effect/handlers ctx)\n                 (yrt.effect/raise ctx :root on-empty)))]\n    (doseq [backend (keys h/backends), bundled? [true false]]\n      (testing (str backend \" bundled=\" bundled?)\n        (is (= [:normal :orelse [:caught :boom] 3 4 5\n                [[:inner :boom] [:outer :boom] :finally-normal :escape]\n                nil [:empty :root]]\n               (run-runtime backend bundled? form)))))))\n\n\n(deftest resumable-control\n  (let [form\n        '(let [ctx (cell/new (yrt.effect/ctx nil 0 0 nil))\n               log (cell/new [])\n               note (fn [v] (cell/set! log (conj (cell/get log) v)))\n               unhandled (fn [tag payload] (conj [] tag payload))\n               resumed (yrt.effect/handle ctx :test\n                         (fn [payload k] (do (note :resume-handler) (k (+ 2 payload))))\n                         (fn []\n                           (yrt.effect/try-finally ctx\n                             (fn []\n                               (let [v (yrt.effect/perform ctx :test 10 unhandled)]\n                                 (do (note :resumed) (+ 1 v))))\n                             note :resume-cleanup)))\n               aborted (yrt.effect/handle ctx :test\n                         (fn [payload k] (do (note :abort-handler) payload))\n                         (fn []\n                           (yrt.effect/try-finally ctx\n                             (fn []\n                               (yrt.effect/handle ctx :unrelated\n                                 (fn [payload k] (note :unexpected-handler))\n                                 (fn []\n                                   (do (yrt.effect/perform ctx :test :aborted unhandled)\n                                       (note :unreachable)))))\n                             (fn [e] (note :abort-cleanup))\n                             :unused)))\n               thrown (yrt.effect/try-value ctx\n                        (fn []\n                          (yrt.effect/handle ctx :test\n                            (fn [payload k] (yrt.effect/raise ctx payload (fn [e] :unexpected)))\n                            (fn []\n                              (yrt.effect/try-finally ctx\n                                (fn [] (yrt.effect/perform ctx :test :handler-error unhandled))\n                                note :unused))))\n                        (fn [e] e))]\n           (conj [] resumed aborted thrown (cell/get log) (yrt.effect/handlers ctx)\n                 (yrt.effect/perform ctx :no-handler 2 unhandled)))]\n    (doseq [backend (keys h/backends), bundled? [true false]]\n      (testing (str backend \" bundled=\" bundled?)\n        (is (= [13 :aborted :handler-error\n                [:resume-handler :resumed :resume-cleanup :abort-handler :abort-cleanup :handler-error]\n                nil [:no-handler 2]]\n               (run-runtime backend bundled? form)))\n        (is (thrown? #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error)\n              (run-runtime backend bundled?\n                '(let [ctx (cell/new (yrt.effect/ctx nil 0 0 nil))\n                       saved (cell/new nil)]\n                   (do (yrt.effect/handle ctx :test\n                         (fn [payload k] (do (cell/set! saved k) (k payload)))\n                         (fn [] (yrt.effect/perform ctx :test 1 (fn [tag p] nil))))\n                       ((cell/get saved) 2))))))))))\n\n\n(deftest integer-policy-and-scanners\n  (let [form\n        '(let [ctx (cell/new (yrt.effect/ctx nil 0 0 nil))\n               bit (yrt.effect/handle ctx :int/bit-limit\n                     (fn [reason k] (k (conj [] :bit reason)))\n                     (fn [] (yrt.int/check-limit ctx (integer/pow 2 100001))))\n               digit (yrt.effect/handle ctx :int/digit-limit\n                       (fn [reason k] (conj [] :digit reason))\n                       (fn [] (yrt.int/check-limit ctx :yin.vm.integer/digit-limit)))\n               float (yrt.effect/handle ctx :math/overflow\n                       (fn [reason k] (conj [] :float reason))\n                       (fn [] (yrt.int/check-limit ctx :yin.vm.integer/float-overflow)))\n               cs [48 48 70 102 33]]\n           (conj [] (yrt.int/check-limit ctx 19) bit digit float\n                 (yrt.int/check-limit-with :yin.vm.integer/digit-limit\n                   (fn [r] :wrong) (fn [r] :digit) (fn [r] :wrong))\n                 (yrt.int/wrap-unsigned -1 256 255)\n                 (yrt.int/wrap-unsigned -257 256 nil)\n                 (yrt.int/wrap-signed 255 128 256)\n                 (yrt.int/in-range? -128 -128 127)\n                 (yrt.int/all-digits? cs 0 4 16)\n                 (yrt.int/all-digits? cs 0 5 16)\n                 (yrt.int/scan-digits cs 0 5 16 0)\n                 (yrt.int/skip-zeros cs 0 5)))]\n    (doseq [backend (keys h/backends), bundled? [true false]]\n      (testing (str backend \" bundled=\" bundled?)\n        (is (= [19 [:bit :yin.vm.integer/bit-limit]\n                [:digit :yin.vm.integer/digit-limit]\n                [:float :yin.vm.integer/float-overflow]\n                :digit 255 255 -1 true true false 255 2]\n               (run-runtime backend bundled? form)))\n        (is (= :zero-division\n               (try\n                 (run-runtime backend bundled?\n                   '(let [ctx (cell/new (yrt.effect/ctx nil 0 0 nil))]\n                      (yrt.effect/try-value ctx\n                        (fn [] (yrt.int/check-limit ctx (integer/floor-div-mod 1 0)))\n                        (fn [error] :caught))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
