{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '554,585p' docs/design/yang.preludes.md && sed -n '3840,3905p' docs/design/yang.antlr.md && nl -ba src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc | sed -n '1080,1160p;1210,1255p'\"","aggregated_output":"### 7.4 Unified trusted `clj` callable bridge, cross-unit admission, and §8.10.7 validation\n\nUnder the Owner Clean-Slate Directive, all Clojure-family §8.10.7 callable/provenance bridging is unified directly into **trusted Layer-2b `clj`** (`src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc`, requiring `yang.call` and `yrt.effect`) — eliminating both any separate `clj.bridge` module and `yang.clojure`'s legacy `dsg__call_token` / inline provenance code in P3:\n\n- `clj` owns the private provenance doors (`cell/dsg__new-provenance`, `cell/dsg__provenance`) inside **both** its linked (`module-uast`) and bundled (`uast`) emitters, never exporting them and keeping them strictly out of `yrt.*`, `clj.py`, `clojure.core.impl`, and `clojure.core`.\n- `clj` exports collision-free primitive helpers **`clj/prim-get`** and **`clj/prim-assoc`**. **Bundled-mode door enforcement (r8, VM-engineer review):** in bundled mode the door effects are honored ONLY for the emitted `clj` definition addresses — the VM admits a provenance-door call by the calling definition's recorded address, never by name resolution from guest scope, so a forged co-bundled call cannot mint provenance (linked mode already gates by content address/admission).\n- **Source-level callable admission (`clj/admitted-callable?`):** Nested `if` verifying `(data/map? x)`, `(= (get x :type) :cell-ref)`, `(cell/authentic? x)`, `(data/callable? (yang.call/entry x))`, and `(yang.call/eligible? x)`. Plain maps, unauthenticated cell-ref maps, and raw host primitives fail cleanly.\n- **Two-step cell-backed callable constructor (`clj/make-callable`):** Allocates `owner = (cell/new meta)` first, installs `entry` closing over `owner` via `cell/set!`, and returns `owner`.\n- **Full 4-step §8.10.7 entry boundary:**\n  - *Step A:* Verify `(data/map? invocation)` and `(data/callable? (get invocation :yang.call/raise))` (fail operationally otherwise).\n  - *Step B:* Outside `try-value`, verify `(yang.call/valid-invocation? invocation)` and `(= (get invocation :yang.call/callee) owner)`; build condition evidence via evaluated `assoc` calls and transfer `:yang.call/invalid-invocation` on failure.\n  - *Step C:* Outside `try-value`, reject unsupported `:yang.call/binding-profile` via evaluated `assoc` evidence and transfer `:yang.call/unsupported-binding`.\n  - *Step D:* Run argument binding + body inside **`yrt.effect/try-value`** on `(clj/rt-ctx)`. Normal exit restores `(clj/rt-ctx)` and returns the value verbatim; escape inspects private `(cell/dsg__provenance e)` to forward retained protocol conditions without double-wrapping or wrap user escapes via `(yang.call/thrown e)`.\n- **Call-site boundary (`clj/invoke-callable`):** Checks `clj/admitted-callable?` (minting retained `:yang.call/not-callable` on failure), else calls `yang.call/invoke` with a `raise-exit` that unwraps `:yang.call/thrown` and retains all other protocol conditions via private `cell/dsg__new-provenance`.\n\n### 7.5 Two-module portable `clojure.core` contract (`clojure.core.impl` + `clojure.core`)\n\nIn Slice P3, the portable Clojure standard library splits into two Layer-2c linker modules — eliminating store-key collisions against VM primitives while publishing cell-free 0-arg export accessors:\n\n1. **`clojure.core.impl` (pure, stateless implementation module — banned from `:ambient-projections`):**\n   - Requires `yang.call`, `clj`, `yrt.int` (zero direct provenance doors; **zero state cells**). Its guest **policy tags** (`:coll/unsupported-key`, `:math/*`, `:int/*`) live in the handler contract installed by the owning entry (`clj.py/run-main` at P3′, plain `yang.clojure`'s own cold-error policy at P2′) — they are NOT part of the linker-derived VM effect footprint; only the underlying **VM effects** its definitions perform are declared through the existing linker footprint mechanism (`yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc`). Host dependencies: `kind` (with `kind/namespace`), `data` (with `float64?`, `equiv`, `admit-key?`, `canonical-compare`, `canonical-entries`), `integer` (`:min-bits 53`), `float`, and `cell` (for cell checks/updates only).\n   - **Zero bare primitive store collisions:** Every definition is prefixed `impl-*` (`impl-identity`, `impl-get`, `impl-assoc`, `impl-conj`, etc.), so internal calls to `(get m k)`, `(assoc m k v)`, `(conj xs x)`, `(first xs)`, `(rest xs)`, `(vec xs)`, `(nil? x)`, `(empty? xs)`, `(not b)` resolve directly to VM primitives.\n   - **Cell-safe collection predicates:** `impl-cell-ref?` ensures authenticated callable cells answer **`false`** to all of `coll?`, `map?`, `set?`, `vector?`, `sequential?`, `seq?`, `list?`, and `reduced?`; `impl-fn?` matches `clj/admitted-callable?` 1-to-1.\n   - **Host-backed portable operations (zero guest-UAST leak workarounds):**\n     - `impl-inc`, `impl-dec`, `impl-rem`, `impl-int?`: delegate to `integer/*` + `yrt.int/check-limit` and `float/add`/`float/sub`.\n     - `impl-not=`: delegates to `(not (data/equiv a b))`.\n     - `impl-str`: deterministic renderer delegating ints to `integer/format`, floats to `float/format`, keywords/symbols to `kind/namespace` + `kind/name`, maps/sets to `data/canonical-entries`, and authenticated cells to `\"#<fn>\"`.\n     - `impl-seq`, `impl-first`, `impl-rest`, `impl-vec`, `impl-keys`, `impl-vals`, `impl-reduce`, `impl-map`, `impl-filter`, `impl-remove`, `impl-into`, `impl-merge`, `impl-union`, `impl-difference`: normalize maps/sets via `data/canonical-entries`.\n     - Map/set mutators and lookups (`impl-assoc`, `impl-get`, `impl-contains?`, `impl-conj`, `impl-disj`, `impl-merge`, `impl-into`, etc.): enforce `data/admit-key?`.\n     - Explicitly excluded: `var?`, `resolve`, `invoke-value`.\n2. **Public cell-free facade `clojure.core` (`src/cljc/yang/clojure/core_module.cljc`):**\n   - Requires `clj` and `clojure.core.impl`. Exports only cell-free pure functions at install time: idempotent 0-arg `init!` (building `{sym cell}` with `clj/prim-assoc` and `clj/make-callable`), 1-arg `export` (using `clj/prim-get`), and 0-arg cell-accessor exports `(fn [] (clojure.core/export (quote <name>)))`.\n\n#### 8.10.7 Normal return and escaping conditions\n\nNormal return is the value of ordinary Yin application. There is no\nextra return continuation, completion packet around each result, or new\nlanguage-specific return instruction.\n\nAn escaping source exception invokes the supplied raise exit with:\n\n```clojure\n{:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown\n :yang.call/value  original-thrown-value}\n```\n\nThis is the argument to an exceptional continuation transfer, not an\nordinary return. Returning an identical-looking map returns normal data.\nLikewise, a source program throwing a map with these keys throws that\nmap as the **payload of a new condition**; its shape is never evidence\nthat it is already a condition to forward. No engine-effect value is\nsynthesized.\n\nProtocol failures use qualified reasons such as\n`:yang.call/not-callable`, `:yang.call/invalid-invocation`, and\n`:yang.call/unsupported-binding`, with plain evidence. The caller maps\nthem to a documented local exception form retaining the complete\noriginal condition. Callee argument-binding failures retain the actual\ncallee exception under `:yang.call/thrown`. These reasons do not extend\n`dao.stream`'s outcome algebra.\n\nThe receiving caller interprets an escaping exception as follows:\n\n1. A payload valid as an exception in its own runtime retains that\n   runtime's ordinary catching and identity behavior.\n2. A runtime permitting arbitrary thrown values, such as JavaScript,\n   may deliver the original payload directly.\n3. A runtime requiring exception objects, such as Python or PHP,\n   represents an otherwise foreign payload with its own\n   `ForeignException`, retaining the complete condition and original\n   payload. Catch-all catches this local object. Typed source catches\n   match its local hierarchy, never guessed foreign class names.\n\n`ForeignException` is a proposed prelude-owned type, not a VM type.\nUnchanged rethrow propagates the original condition without adding\nwrappers. Raising a new exception creates a new condition. Crossing back\ninto a runtime recognizing the original exception restores its original\ntype and identity. Formatting a foreign payload must not implicitly\ninvoke a foreign method.\n\nThe runtime associates its generated wrapper's identity with the retained\ncondition for the wrapper's entire lifetime, separate from source-writable\nattributes. The association normally lives in private wrapper-cell\ncontents, or an equivalent task-owned identity structure with the same\nlifetime. It survives storing or returning the wrapper after the creating\ncall/catch activation has ended, and remains recoverable when that same\nwrapper is rethrown in another activation. Temporary catch state alone is\ninsufficient. Reachability/reclamation must retain the condition and its\npayload while the wrapper is live, without an ambient registry.\n\nThe runtime must not detect wrappers or unwrap arbitrary maps by their\nkey names. JavaScript may expose raw payloads for\n`:yang.call/thrown`; its local exception for a protocol failure must still\nretain that failure's qualified condition. Rethrowing the same generated\nexception forwards that complete condition, including protocol reasons;\nthrowing an unrelated value creates a new `:yang.call/thrown` condition.\nSaved activation state refers to this identity-owned association; exiting\nor restoring a catch does not destroy it.\n  1080\t   `fn-name` (or the anonymous fn's `source`) instead.\"\n  1081\t  [env fn-name source arities]\n  1082\t  (let [counts (map :n arities)]\n  1083\t    (when (not= (count counts) (count (set counts)))\n  1084\t      (reject! \"Two arities with the same parameter count\" {:counts (vec counts)}))\n  1085\t    (reduce (fn [else {:keys [n form]}]\n  1086\t              (list 'if\n  1087\t                    (list 'data/content= (list 'data/count av-sym) n)\n  1088\t                    form\n  1089\t                    else))\n  1090\t            (if (outcomes? env) (arity-error-form fn-name source) (list 'data/count))\n  1091\t            (reverse arities))))\n  1092\t\n  1093\t\n  1094\t(defn- check-av-params!\n  1095\t  [params]\n  1096\t  (when-not (vector? params)\n  1097\t    (reject! \"fn parameters must be a vector\" {:params params}))\n  1098\t  (doseq [p params]\n  1099\t    (when (= '& p)\n  1100\t      (reject! \"Variadic fn parameters are not supported\" {:params params}))\n  1101\t    (check-binder! p params)))\n  1102\t\n  1103\t\n  1104\t(defn- admit-call-descriptor\n  1105\t  \"Allocate a descriptor supplied by trusted UAST/profile code.\"\n  1106\t  [descriptor-ast tail?]\n  1107\t  (cond-> (u/app (u/v 'cell/new) descriptor-ast)\n  1108\t    tail? (assoc :tail? true)))\n  1109\t\n  1110\t\n  1111\t(defn- compile-call-descriptor\n  1112\t  \"Publish a private argument-vector body through the clj entry boundary.\"\n  1113\t  [body-ast tail?]\n  1114\t  (let [meta (cond-> {:clj/type :function}\n  1115\t               (= 2 (count (:params body-ast))) (assoc :clj/tail-call? true))]\n  1116\t    (cond-> (u/app (u/v 'clj/make-callable) (u/lit meta) body-ast)\n  1117\t      tail? (assoc :tail? true))))\n  1118\t\n  1119\t\n  1120\t(defn- compile-av-fn\n  1121\t  \"Compile arities [{:params :body}] to one closure over an argument vector.\n  1122\t   `fn-name` names the function in an arity error outcome. Under the outcome\n  1123\t   model the published value is an immutable common-call descriptor.\"\n  1124\t  ([arities env tail? macro-env] (compile-av-fn arities env tail? macro-env nil nil))\n  1125\t  ([arities env tail? macro-env fn-name] (compile-av-fn arities env tail? macro-env fn-name nil))\n  1126\t  ([arities env tail? macro-env fn-name source]\n  1127\t   (let [arities (mapv (fn [{:keys [params body]}]\n  1128\t                         (check-av-params! params)\n  1129\t                         {:n (count params)\n  1130\t                          :form (av-let env macro-env params body)})\n  1131\t                       arities)\n  1132\t         tail-call? (volatile! false)\n  1133\t         body (compile-lambda [av-sym] (av-dispatch env fn-name source arities)\n  1134\t                              (cond-> (dissoc env ::tail-call?)\n  1135\t                                (outcomes? env) (assoc ::tail-call? tail-call?))\n  1136\t                              false macro-env)\n  1137\t         body (cond-> body\n  1138\t                @tail-call? (update :params conj 'dsg__tail_invoke))]\n  1139\t     (if (outcomes? env)\n  1140\t       (compile-call-descriptor body tail?)\n  1141\t       (cond-> body tail? (assoc :tail? true))))))\n  1142\t\n  1143\t\n  1144\t(defn- fn-arities\n  1145\t  \"Arities of (fn [params] body*) or (fn ([params] body*)+) operands.\"\n  1146\t  [operands]\n  1147\t  (cond\n  1148\t    (vector? (first operands))\n  1149\t    [{:params (first operands), :body (rest operands)}]\n  1150\t\n  1151\t    (and (seq operands) (every? #(and (seq? %) (vector? (first %))) operands))\n  1152\t    (mapv (fn [a] {:params (first a), :body (rest a)}) operands)\n  1153\t\n  1154\t    :else (reject! \"fn parameters must be a vector\" {:params (first operands)})))\n  1155\t\n  1156\t\n  1157\t(defn- adapter-counts\n  1158\t  \"The argument counts an adapter for native `sym` admits: the fixed arities\n  1159\t   of its `:yin.k/arities` profile, extended to `adapter-variadic-cap` when\n  1160\t   the profile is `:variadic`. A name with no declared profile admits\n  1210\t    (u/if-node (u/app (u/v 'data/content=)\n  1211\t                      (u/app (u/v 'clj/prim-get) callee (u/lit :