{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_55","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '644,649p' docs/design/yang.preludes.md | fold -w 170\nsed -n '670,804p;1885,1948p;1970,2060p' src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\ngit show HEAD\"'^:src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc | sed -n '\"'1379,1396p;2175,2233p'\nrg -n 'dsg__intra_call|dsg__call_token|budget' test/yang/{clojure_callsite_test.cljc,rt/effect_test.cljc}\"","aggregated_output":"| Slice | Scope & deliverables | Golden impact | Concrete acceptance gate |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **P0′ — Composition plumbing & `:pure` host core extensions** | Implement `:yang.prelude/recipe` / `:yang.prelude/profile`, `validate-profile` + `admit-profile` **in `y\nang.core.prelude-admission`** (3→5 publics, per the §5.2 home rule); add `:pure` host exports (`data/float64?`, `data/equiv`, `data/admit-key?`, `data/canonical-compare`,\n `data/canonical-entries`, `kind/namespace`, and boxed `yin.vm.float` across all 4 hosts); consolidate `defquoted` into `yang.core.defquoted` (dedicated host macro namesp\nace, keeping `yang.core.prelude` at 11 publics — naming per r8 M9, consistent across §8.1/§8.2); base-prelude emitter recipes record the *current* per-prelude modes as mi\ngration truth (`:linear` for `py`, `:balanced` for `php`/`js`; the bundled `yang.clojure` continuation family is a LEFT FOLD, not balanced — recorded as its own mode so t\nhe freeze is exact) without changing shapes. | No golden churn for py/js/php (no shape change); new modules get fresh addresses | Closure, missing-manifest, `host-limits`\n, direct-provenance vs. transitive-footprint tests; 4-host test suite for `data/equiv` (`[0.0] == [-0.0]`, `[NaN] != [NaN]`, `(keyword nil \"a/b\") != (keyword \"a\" \"b\")`), \n`data/admit-key?`, `data/canonical-compare`/`canonical-entries`, and `yin.vm.float` (`2.1 // 0.7 == 3.0`, `-0.0 // 2.0 == -0.0`, `0.5 ** -2000 -> :underflow`, `format` `1\n.0 -> \"1.0\"`); existing py/php oracle suites unchanged-green. |\n| **P1′ — `yrt.effect` + `yrt.int` with Clojure-only consumers; unified trusted `clj`** | Implement stateless `yrt.effect` (5-slot `data/nth` frames, abortive `raise`/`tr\ny-value`/`try-orelse`/`try-finally`/`call-ec`, plus resumable `handle`/`perform` — the frame design anticipates py/php `:depth` accounting but only clj/clj.py exercise it\n) and `yrt.int`; upgrade `clj` to the unified trusted form (two-step `make-callable`, evaluated `assoc` conditions, `invoke-callable`, `prim-get`/`prim-assoc`, retiring `\nyang.clojure`'s `dsg__call_token` / inline provenance ops); add `dsg__add`/`dsg__lte` for bundled `clj`. **py/js/php preludes untouched** — they keep their own mechanisms\n. | Refresh `clj`/`yang.clojure` goldens cleanly; py/js/php goldens untouched | `yrt.effect` unit tests (abortive, `finally`, resumable one-shot `handle`/`perform`, cold \npolicy traps) across semantic/stack/register VMs; bundled/linked `yang.clojure` parity under shadowed `(defn get ...)`; clj-only synthetic nonzero depth/base fixtures exe\nrcising the `:depth` slot; independent concurrent `clj` tasks sharing `yrt.*`; bundled == linked + 4-host; `clj ./bin/analyze-deps.clj` clean. (H7 repair: native collecti\non invocation — including the landed fixture where a locally bound map invoked with `:k` returns 9, which requires the native data-call dispatch to admit locally bound ma\nps — and bundled primitive shadowing through the new standard library gate in the P2′ row below; the REAL cross-syntax `clj → clj.py → clj` unwind with cleanup and contex\nt restoration gates SOLELY in the P3′ row.) |\n| **P2′ — Unified `clojure.core` + `yang.clojure` migration** | Publish collision-free `clojure.core.impl` (pure, `impl-*` prefix, `admit-key?`-guarded) + cell-free `cloj\nure.core` facade; migrate `yang.clojure` directly onto unified `clj` + `clojure.core`. | Refresh `yang.clojure` goldens cleanly | Native collection invocation through the\n new standard library (the locally-bound-map `:k` → 9 fixture) and bundled primitive shadowing of bare `get`/`assoc` (which otherwise resolve through the source store bef\nore VM primitives); unified `yang.clojure` suite green. The real `clj → clj.py → clj` cross-syntax unwind (cleanup + context restoration) gates ONLY at P3′, after `clj.py\n` exists. |\n| **P3′ — Descriptor parameterization + `clj.py` + `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` (the DEFAULT flip)** | Implement generic `yang.core.semantics` with UAST-derived arity &\n role validation; define the python frontend contract; refactor `yang.python.antlr.lower` to read literals/hooks/capabilities from `:yang.semantics/descriptor` (the legac\ny `py-v1` descriptor pins today's `'py/*` hooks 1:1 — behavior-preserving, gated by the existing CPython oracle suites); publish `clj.py`; flip `yang.python`'s default `r\nuntime-profile` to `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` (a revision re-pin in `yang.frontend`). | py goldens regenerate under the descriptor-driven path (legacy descriptor byte\n-identical outcomes); clojure-core-v1 gets fresh goldens | Legacy-descriptor behavior preservation: full CPython corpus + 4-host parity under `py-v1` pin; end-to-end 4-ho\nst `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` suite (numeric/float ops, `:max-bits 53` limit traps, `data/admit-key?` refusals, `data/equiv`, `data/canonical-entries` ordering, deter\nministic `str`/`gensym`); the cross-syntax `clj → clj.py → clj` unwind gate — cleanup and context restoration, exactly once per activation — listed directly here; capabil\nity refusal tests (typed `except E:`, `genexpr` under `:control/generators :refused`); default-profile regressions (r8): an unqualified `:k` key admits successfully (the \nnamespace-non-empty rule applies to two-part keywords only); equal exact integers in different host carriers hit the same map entry on insert AND lookup; a local/projecte\nd value equal to `:clj/unbound` remains distinguishable from an absent binding; canonical traversal order matches Jing encoded-byte order (`0` before `nil`); UAST-derived\n validation rejecting wrong arity, non-lambda hooks, unqualified hooks, reserved doors, out-of-closure exports. |\n       :arities [{:params (first more), :body (rest more)}]}\n\n      (and (seq? (first more)) (vector? (ffirst more)))\n      (let [arities (take-while seq? more)\n            trailing (drop (count arities) more)]\n        (when (and (seq trailing)\n                   (not (and (map? (first trailing)) (nil? (next trailing)))))\n          (reject! \"Unexpected forms after fn arities\" {:name fn-name}))\n        {:name fn-name, :meta (merge header (first trailing))\n         :arities (mapv (fn [a]\n                          (when-not (vector? (first a))\n                            (reject! \"Malformed fn arity\" {:name fn-name}))\n                          {:params (first a), :body (rest a)})\n                        arities)})\n\n      :else\n      (reject! (str \"Malformed \" operator \" form\") {:name fn-name}))))\n\n\n(declare compile-fn compile-av-fn)\n\n\n(defn- compile-defn\n  \"Compile a defn form natively to a yin/def application: the tree the\n   expander's standard `defn` also produces. This path is used only when no\n   defmacro named defn is in scope. Several arities need the argument-vector\n   convention: a plain Yin closure nil-fills missing arguments and drops\n   extras, so it cannot observe the call's argument count.\"\n  [operator operands env tail? macro-env]\n  (let [{fn-name :name, header :meta, :keys [arities]} (parse-defn operator operands)\n        fn-ast (if (::convention env)\n                 (compile-av-fn arities env false macro-env fn-name)\n                 (do (when (< 1 (count arities))\n                       (reject! \"Multi-arity fn is not supported: closures cannot observe argument count\"\n                                {:name fn-name, :arities (count arities)}))\n                     (let [{:keys [params body]} (first arities)]\n                       (compile-fn params body env false macro-env))))\n        ast (cond-> {:type :application\n                     :operator {:type :variable, :name 'yin/def}\n                     :operands [{:type :literal, :value (strip-symbol-meta fn-name)}\n                                fn-ast]}\n              tail? (assoc :tail? true))]\n    (if (seq header)\n      (vary-meta ast merge header)\n      ast)))\n\n\n(defn- check-macro-params!\n  \"Every macro parameter is a plain symbol outside the reserved prefix; an\n   & must be followed by exactly one binder.\"\n  [params]\n  (doseq [p params :when (not= '& p)]\n    (check-binder! p params)\n    (when-not (symbol? p)\n      (reject! \"defmacro parameters must be plain symbols\" {:params params})))\n  (when-let [i (first (keep-indexed (fn [i p] (when (= '& p) i)) params))]\n    (when-not (= (+ i 2) (count params))\n      (reject! \"& needs exactly one binder in defmacro parameters\" {:params params}))))\n\n\n(defn- compile-defmacro\n  \"Lower (defmacro name doc? attr-map? [params] body*) to ordinary\n   (yin/def name (fn ...)) syntax. The lambda is flagged `:macro?` for the\n   encoder's declaration row (yin.vm.macro.md §10.2); projection drops the\n   flag from the row.\"\n  [operands env tail? macro-env]\n  (let [{fn-name :name, :keys [doc attrs more]} (parse-head 'defmacro operands)\n        params (first more)\n        _ (when-not (vector? params)\n            (reject! \"defmacro needs a parameter vector\" {:name fn-name}))\n        _ (check-macro-params! params)\n        header (merge (when doc {:doc doc}) attrs)\n        ast (cond-> {:type :application\n                     :operator {:type :variable, :name 'yin/def}\n                     :operands [{:type :literal, :value (strip-symbol-meta fn-name)}\n                                (assoc (compile-lambda params (body-expression (rest more))\n                                                       env false macro-env)\n                                       :macro? true)]}\n              tail? (assoc :tail? true))]\n    (if (seq header)\n      (vary-meta ast merge header)\n      ast)))\n\n\n(defn special-form?\n  \"Check if a form is a special form.\"\n  [form]\n  (and (seq? form)\n       (symbol? (first form))\n       (contains? #{'fn 'if 'let 'quote 'do 'def 'dao.stream.apply/call 'defmacro 'loop 'recur} (first form))))\n\n\n(defn compile-literal\n  \"Compile a literal value to Universal AST.\"\n  [form _tail?]\n  {:type :literal, :value form})\n\n\n(defn compile-variable\n  \"Compile a variable reference (symbol) to Universal AST.\"\n  [sym _tail?]\n  {:type :variable, :name sym})\n\n\n(defn compile-def\n  \"Compile a def form to Universal AST.\n   Emits a yin/def application which requires environment support.\"\n  ([sym value env tail?] (compile-def sym value env tail? initial-macro-env))\n  ([sym value env tail? macro-env]\n   (check-def-name! 'def sym)\n   (cond-> {:type :application,\n            :operator {:type :variable, :name 'yin/def},\n            :operands [{:type :literal, :value sym}\n                       (compile-form value false env macro-env)]}\n     tail? (assoc :tail? true))))\n\n\n(defn compile-lambda\n  \"Compile a lambda (fn) expression to Universal AST.\n\n  Clojure: (fn [x y] (+ x y))\n  AST: {:type :lambda\n        :params [x y]\n        :body <compiled-body>}\"\n  ([params body env tail?] (compile-lambda params body env tail? initial-macro-env))\n  ([params body env tail? macro-env]\n   (let [new-macro-env (shadow-macro-env macro-env params)\n         ;; a source fn boundary resets the recur target\n         compiled-body (compile-form body true\n                                     (with-locals (dissoc env ::target) params)\n                                     new-macro-env)]\n     (cond-> {:type :lambda, :params (vec params), :body compiled-body}\n       tail? (assoc :tail? true)))))\n\n\n     (compile-form-1 form tail? env macro-env)\n     (binding [*call-site-finalizing* true]\n       (annotate-call-sites (compile-form-1 form tail? env macro-env))))))\n\n\n(defn- program-env\n  \"The compile-time env of one program. Without `opts` it is empty: the\n   native path. `{:convention :arg-vector, :native #{symbol}, :macros\n   #{symbol}}` opts into the argument-vector convention: `:native` names the\n   primitives a bare symbol may call directly (a set, or a map from name to\n   its published profile, whose `:yin.k/arities` give an adapter its admitted\n   counts), `:macros` the expander-side\n   macro names whose calls must stay ordinary applications. The program's\n   own top-level definitions are never native. `:outcomes true` selects the\n   continuation lane (see its section); the `:adapters` opt is accepted for\n   compatibility but no longer consulted — the outcome adapters are retired.\"\n  [forms opts]\n  (if-not opts\n    {}\n    (do (when-not (= :arg-vector (:convention opts))\n          (reject! \"Unknown compile-program convention\" {:opts opts}))\n        (when-let [hit (seq (filter control-heads (:macros opts)))]\n          (reject! \"A :macros entry names a compiler form\" {:macros (vec hit)}))\n        (let [defined (into #{}\n                            (keep (fn [f]\n                                    (when (and (seq? f)\n                                               (contains? #{'def 'defn 'defn- 'defmacro} (first f))\n                                               (symbol? (second f)))\n                                      (strip-symbol-meta (second f)))))\n                            forms)]\n          ;; the compiler emits bare conj and vec (collection literals, apply),\n          ;; so a program definition of either would capture them\n          (when-let [hit (first (filter #{'conj 'vec} defined))]\n            (reject! (str \"Defining \" hit \" would capture the argument-vector constructor\")\n                     {:name hit}))\n          (cond-> {::convention {:native (set (if (map? (:native opts))\n                                                (keys (:native opts))\n                                                (:native opts)))\n                                 :arities (into {}\n                                                (keep (fn [[sym profile]]\n                                                        (when-let [a (if (map? profile)\n                                                                       (:yin.k/arities profile)\n                                                                       profile)]\n                                                          [sym a])))\n                                                (when (map? (:native opts)) (:native opts)))\n                                 :macros (set (:macros opts))}\n                   ::defined defined\n                   ::invoker (boolean (some #(and (seq? %) (= 'defn (first %))\n                                                  (= 'invoke-value (second %))\n                                                  (:yin.k/invoker (meta (second %)))) forms))}\n            (:outcomes opts) (assoc ::outcomes {:adapters (or (:adapters opts) {})}))))))\n\n\n(defn- check-program-symbols!\n  \"The program pre-pass. Quoted data is exempt. The reserved prefix names\n   compiler temporaries, so no user symbol may carry it in ANY position\n   (binder, reference, definition name); `loop` and `recur` are special forms,\n   so they may only head a list, never stand as a value or a binder.\"\n  [form]\n  (cond\n    (symbol? form)\n    (do (when (reserved-name? form)\n          (reject! \"Symbol uses the reserved destructuring prefix\"\n                   {:symbol form, :prefix reserved-prefix}))\n    form\n    (lower-function-body env macro-env [] [form])))\n\n\n(defn- with-runtime\n  \"Wrap a unit in its clj entry boundary and install the bundled runtime.\"\n  [ast linked?]\n  (let [unit (u/app (u/v 'clj/run-unit) (u/lam [] ast))\n        helpers (u/let1 'dsg__ex_message (u/sexp->uast ex-message-form)\n                        (u/let1 'dsg__ex_data (u/sexp->uast ex-data-form) unit))]\n    (if linked?\n      helpers\n      (u/then prelude/bundled-uast helpers))))\n\n\n(defn compile-program\n  \"Compile a sequence of Clojure forms into a single Universal AST.\n   Top-level defs compile to explicit yin/def store writes, sequenced via lambda.\n   Top-level defmacros are lowered to ordinary (yin/def name (fn ...)) syntax\n   with :macro? true on the lambda; the encoder turns that flag into a\n   declaration row and the expander, not this compiler, recognizes calls.\n   The three-argument form takes `opts` opting into the argument-vector\n   convention (see `program-env`); without it the output is the native one.\"\n  ([forms] (compile-program forms true))\n  ([forms tail?] (compile-program forms tail? nil))\n  ([forms tail? opts]\n   (run! check-program-symbols! forms)\n   (let [env (program-env forms opts)]\n     ;; A discarded definition must not become a lexical binding in the\n     ;; following definitions. Descriptor entry and body closures both capture\n     ;; their environment: retaining the previous descriptor here doubles its\n     ;; paths at each definition during machine-data validation and UCF lift.\n     (letfn [(discard-result\n               [ast]\n               (if (outcomes? env) (u/then ast (u/lit nil)) ast))\n             (go\n               [forms macro-env]\n               (if (empty? forms)\n                 (compile-literal nil tail?)\n                 (let [head       (cond->> (first forms)\n                                    (outcomes? env) (lower-top-form env macro-env))\n                       rest-forms (rest forms)]\n                   (cond\n                     ;; defmacro: ordinary (yin/def name (fn ...)) syntax whose\n                     ;; lambda the encoder declares; later forms see the name\n                     ;; only so the native defn lowering can yield to it.\n                     (and (seq? head) (= 'defmacro (first head)))\n                     (let [defined (compile-defmacro (rest head) env false macro-env)]\n                       (cond-> {:type     :application\n                                :operator {:type :lambda, :params ['_]\n                                           :body (go rest-forms\n                                                     (assoc macro-env\n                                                            (strip-symbol-meta (second head))\n                                                            {:type :user}))}\n                                :operands [(discard-result defined)]}\n                         tail? (assoc :tail? true)))\n                     ;; def: sequence with current macro-env\n                     (and (seq? head) (= 'def (first head)))\n                     (let [[_ name value] head\n                           value (if (outcomes? env)\n                                   (lower-function-body env macro-env [] [value])\n                                   value)]\n                       (cond-> {:type     :application\n                                :operator {:type :lambda, :params ['_]\n                                           :body (go rest-forms macro-env)}\n                                :operands [(discard-result (compile-def name value env false macro-env))]}\n                         tail? (assoc :tail? true)))\n                     ;; single form\n                     (= 1 (count forms))\n                     (compile-form head tail? (assoc env ::top-level true) macro-env)\n                     ;; sequence\n                     :else\n                     (cond-> {:type     :application\n                              :operator {:type :lambda, :params ['_]\n                                         :body (go rest-forms macro-env)}\n                              :operands [(discard-result\n                                           (compile-form head false\n                                                         (assoc env ::top-level true) macro-env))]}\n                       tail? (assoc :tail? true))))))]\n       (annotate-call-sites\n         (cond->> (go forms initial-macro-env)\n           (outcomes? env) (#(with-runtime % (:linked-runtime opts)))\n           (outcomes? env) tails/remark-tails))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The guest collection and higher-order library (slice 7)\n;; =============================================================================\n;;\n;; Guest-side source, compiled through this compiler like any program: the\n;; functions that invoke guest closures (map, filter, reduce, comp, partial)\n(defn- intra-unit-fn?\n  \"True when `operator` statically names a top-level `defn`/`defn-` of this\n   unit under the outcome model: unshadowed by locals and never defined by\n   `def` or `defmacro`.\"\n  [env operator]\n  (and (outcomes? env)\n       (symbol? operator)\n       (not (contains? (locals env) operator))\n       (contains? (::defined-fns env) operator)))\n\n\n(defn- cell-ref-shaped-node\n  \"The UAST pre-filter for WHEN to ask the heap about a callee: the\n   callee could be a cell reference the VM issued — `:type :cell-ref`\n   with the `:id` and `:seal` every issued reference carries, no other\n   entries, a seal of the issued form (a 64-character string). The\n   shape never decides meaning (ruling of record, rule 2): a map\n   passing it is only worth asking about, and the `cell/authentic?`\n    {}\n    (do (when-not (= :arg-vector (:convention opts))\n          (reject! \"Unknown compile-program convention\" {:opts opts}))\n        (when-let [hit (seq (filter control-heads (:macros opts)))]\n          (reject! \"A :macros entry names a compiler form\" {:macros (vec hit)}))\n        (let [defined (into #{}\n                            (keep (fn [f]\n                                    (when (and (seq? f)\n                                               (contains? #{'def 'defn 'defn- 'defmacro} (first f))\n                                               (symbol? (second f)))\n                                      (strip-symbol-meta (second f)))))\n                            forms)\n              defined-fns (top-level-defined-fns forms (:macros opts))]\n          ;; the compiler emits bare conj and vec (collection literals, apply),\n          ;; so a program definition of either would capture them\n          (when-let [hit (first (filter #{'conj 'vec} defined))]\n            (reject! (str \"Defining \" hit \" would capture the argument-vector constructor\")\n                     {:name hit}))\n          (cond-> {::convention {:native (set (if (map? (:native opts))\n                                                (keys (:native opts))\n                                                (:native opts)))\n                                 :arities (into {}\n                                                (keep (fn [[sym profile]]\n                                                        (when-let [a (if (map? profile)\n                                                                       (:yin.k/arities profile)\n                                                                       profile)]\n                                                          [sym a])))\n                                                (when (map? (:native opts)) (:native opts)))\n                                 :macros (set (:macros opts))}\n                   ::defined defined\n                   ::defined-fns defined-fns\n                   ::invoker (boolean (some #(and (seq? %) (= 'defn (first %))\n                                                  (= 'invoke-value (second %))\n                                                  (:yin.k/invoker (meta (second %)))) forms))}\n            (:outcomes opts) (assoc ::outcomes {:adapters (or (:adapters opts) {})}))))))\n\n\n(defn- check-program-symbols!\n  \"The program pre-pass. Quoted data is exempt. The reserved prefix names\n   compiler temporaries, so no user symbol may carry it in ANY position\n   (binder, reference, definition name); `loop` and `recur` are special forms,\n   so they may only head a list, never stand as a value or a binder.\"\n  [form]\n  (cond\n    (symbol? form)\n    (do (when (reserved-name? form)\n          (reject! \"Symbol uses the reserved destructuring prefix\"\n                   {:symbol form, :prefix reserved-prefix}))\n        (when (and (nil? (namespace form)) (contains? #{'loop 'recur} form))\n          (reject! (str form \" is only legal in operator position\") {:symbol form})))\n    (seq? form)\n    (when-not (= 'quote (first form))\n      (let [head (first form)]\n        (when (and (symbol? head) (reserved-name? head))\n          (reject! \"Symbol uses the reserved destructuring prefix\"\n                   {:symbol head, :prefix reserved-prefix}))\n        (when-not (symbol? head)\n          (check-program-symbols! head))\n        (run! check-program-symbols! (rest form))))\ntest/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc:896:   are supplied data. Kept public so the separately declared budget runner can\ntest/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc:2918:      link whose manifest is `address` spends its budget and stays\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
